* END-HISTORY
*
* START-DESCRIPTION:
*
*    deffun voc_refusal(f) calling '!voc_refusal'
*    n = voc_refusal(file.var)
*
* Returns 0 when a change to the file F is allowed, otherwise the number of the message that says
* why not (11008 the VOC needs ADMIN, 11028 the global catalogue and its siblings need a
* global-password session).  Nothing is displayed.  See !voc_guard for what the rule is for and
* why it is applied by BASIC programs: op_dio3.c refuses a user program's own write, but a verb
* that is $internal passes the C test, so each $internal verb that changes a file its user
* named asks for itself.
*
* IT LOOKS AT THE FILE THAT WAS OPENED, NOT AT THE NAME THAT WAS TYPED, so a Q-pointer to a VOC,
* or "voc" in any case, is caught.  A VOC is a DH (dynamic) file whose last path component is
* "voc" - the same rule as voc_write_refused() in C.  The dictionary, voc.dic, is not the VOC.
*
* END-DESCRIPTION
*
* START-CODE

$internal
function voc_refusal(f)
$catalog !voc_refusal

$include keys.h
$include int$keys.h

   p = downcase(fileinfo(f, FL$PATH))
   if p[len(p), 1] = '/' then p = p[1, len(p) - 1]
   last = field(p, '/', dcount(p, '/'))

*  30 Sep 26 LSOLO 12 - RULING 33 (Windows Solo): SDSYS's gcat, global.bp.out and
*  solo.policy (ruling 34's deny list) are the SD Core server's, changed only
*  by a session signed in with the global password - ADMIN is NOT enough, so
*  this comes before the ADMIN test.  The C gate (op_dio3.c
*  global_write_refused) lets $internal verbs through, and COPY, ED, DELETE and
*  the rest are $internal.  On Linux the SDSYS directory IS the install's home
*  directory (no "sdsys" component), so the test is the full path: @SDSYS plus
*  the name.  A symbolic link to one of them is NOT recognised here - the
*  tree belongs to the Linux user, so this governs what SD will do, not what
*  that user can do to the files from outside SD (op_dio3.c says the same).
   if fileinfo(f, FL$TYPE) = FL$TYPE.DIR then
      sd.dir = downcase(@sdsys)
      if sd.dir[len(sd.dir), 1] = '/' then sd.dir = sd.dir[1, len(sd.dir) - 1]
      if p = sd.dir : '/gcat' or p = sd.dir : '/global.bp.out' or p = sd.dir : '/solo.policy' then
         if kernel(K$GLOBAL.SESSION, -1) then return 0
         return 11028 ;* The global catalogue can only be changed by the SD Core server
      end
   end

   if kernel(K$ADMINISTRATOR, -1) then return 0

   if fileinfo(f, FL$TYPE) # FL$TYPE.DH then return 0

   if last # 'voc' then return 0

   return 11008 ;* The VOC can only be changed after ADMIN
end

* END-CODE
